From 638a4af6545360eb4bc850866054d1b22a7092b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:15:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hv: scrub the Type-C retimer ADT nodes (atcrt*) when running
 over USB

setup_adt() removes the proxy port's dart-usb, atc-phy, usb-drd, acio,
hpm and atc dp nodes so the guest leaves that port alone, but not the
port's Type-C retimer. The retimers are i2c children named atcrt%d
(on t602x: /arm-io/i2c6/atcrt0..2, i2c addresses 0x18..0x1a); their
bus number differs per SoC.

Left in the ADT, macOS binds com.apple.driver.AppleTypeCRetimer on
them and reprograms the retimers about 35 s into the boot. On a J414c
(M2 Max) both traced macOS 13.5 boots ended inside a burst of i2c6
transactions (58 and 53 ps_i2c6 power cycles, nothing else in the last
500 trace lines) with the host side raising pyserial "device reports
readiness to read but returned no data": the retimer on the proxy port
(hpm0/atc-phy0/usb-drd0, dock id 0x183, left-back) was reprogrammed
and the USB link carrying the proxy dropped.

Walk every /arm-io/i2c* node and delete all atcrt* children. The
retimer-to-port index is a naming convention only, and the guest's
other ports are not needed under the hypervisor, so all of them go.
Verified on the J414c ADT with the m1n1 ADT parser: the three nodes
are removed, the tree rebuilds (353612 bytes) and reparses, and the
existing hpm0/atc-phy0 scrub is unchanged.
---
 proxyclient/m1n1/hv/__init__.py | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/proxyclient/m1n1/hv/__init__.py b/proxyclient/m1n1/hv/__init__.py
index 5978593..2396ca0 100644
--- a/proxyclient/m1n1/hv/__init__.py
+++ b/proxyclient/m1n1/hv/__init__.py
@@ -1650,6 +1650,24 @@ class HV(Reloadable):
                 except KeyError:
                     pass
 
+            # The Type-C retimers are i2c children named atcrt%d (i2c6
+            # on t602x; the bus differs per SoC). Left in the ADT,
+            # AppleTypeCRetimer binds them and reprograms the retimers
+            # in a burst of i2c transactions about 35 s into a macOS
+            # boot, which drops the USB link carrying the proxy
+            # (pyserial "readiness without data" on the host). The
+            # retimer-to-port index is a naming convention, so scrub
+            # them all: the guest's other ports are not needed.
+            for i2c in list(self.adt["/arm-io"]):
+                if not i2c.name.startswith("i2c"):
+                    continue
+                for node in list(i2c):
+                    if not node.name.startswith("atcrt"):
+                        continue
+                    name = f"/arm-io/{i2c.name}/{node.name}"
+                    print(f"Removing ADT node {name}")
+                    del self.adt[name]
+
         if self.wdt_cpu is not None:
             name = f"/cpus/cpu{self.wdt_cpu}"
             print(f"Removing ADT node {name}")
-- 
